      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to compute the value of \\(3 \\oplus 1\\) using the given operation \\(\\oplus\\), which is defined as \\(a \\oplus b = 3a + 4b\\).\n\nHere are the steps to find \\(3 \\oplus 1\\):\n\n1. Identify the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) in the expression \\(3 \\oplus 1\\). In this case, \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = 1\\).\n2. Substitute \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = 1\\) into the operation \\(3a + 4b\\):\n   \\[\n   3 \\oplus 1 = 3(3) + 4(1)\n   \\]\n3. Perform the multiplications:\n   \\[\n   3(3) = 9 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 4(1) = 4\n   \\]\n4. Add the results of the multiplications together:\n   \\[\n   9 + 4 = 13\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(3 \\oplus 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{13}\\).",
