      "text": "To solve the problem \\(3 \\oplus 1\\) using the operation defined by \\(a \\oplus b = 3a + 4b\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the given operation and variables:**\n   The operation is defined as:\n   \\[\n   a \\oplus b = 3a + 4b\n   \\]\n   We need to find \\(3 \\oplus 1\\).\n\n2. **Substitute the values into the operation:**\n   Here, \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = 1\\). Substitute these values into the operation:\n   \\[\n   3 \\oplus 1 = 3(3) + 4(1)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   Calculate \\(3 \\times 3\\) and \\(4 \\times 1\\):\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 3 = 9\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 1 = 4\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the results:**\n   Add the results of the multiplications:\n   \\[\n   9 + 4 = 13\n   \\]\n\n5. **Write the final answer:**\n   Therefore, the value of \\(3 \\oplus 1\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{13}\n   \\]",
